<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria offers three floater T-bill issues Monday.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria offers three floater T-bill issues Monday.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry will offer three floating interest T-bill issues with maturities of six, nine and 12 months and a total par of 12 billion levs at auctions on Monday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The issues will be offered with no minimum acceptable prices set in advance.</p>
<p>Interest on the issues is due at maturity. It is set equal to the central bank main interest rate for each of the issues and is adjusted every time the rate is changed by the central bank.</p>
<p>The main interest rate is now set at 4.29 percent monthly. Details of the offers follow:</p>
<p> Issue number	   BG3035997025	 BG3036097023</p>
<p> Maturity		 six months	   nine months</p>
<p> Par value		8.0 bln levs	 2.0 bln</p>
<p> Auction date	   May 26		 May 26</p>
<p> Issue date	     May 28		 May 28</p>
<p> Maturity date	  November 26	  February 25, 1998</p>
<p> Issue number	   BG3036197021</p>
<p> Maturity		 12 months</p>
<p> Par value		2.0 bln levs</p>
<p> Auction date	   May 26</p>
<p> Issue date	     May 28</p>
<p> Maturity date	  May 27, 1998</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
